-- allium: 3
--
-- Effort — what a puzzle takes out of a player
--
-- Scope
--   The second of four models of a player, and the one in which a limit
--   makes things dear. Nothing is hidden and nothing is wrong: every step
--   has a price, the price is the player's own, and a puzzle is rated by
--   what it costs them from the first step to the last. Where the player's
--   profile gives out, the run goes on past it and says so, so that every
--   puzzle the catalogue can finish is priced end to end for every player.
--   reach.allium, lapse.allium and human-solving.allium model the same
--   player differently and none of the four imports another.
--   human-solving.allium also counts effort, from the bottom up: every look,
--   thought and mark is a paid microstep and a price is what they add up to
--   in one seeded attempt. Here a price is read from the top down, off the
--   deduction taken, and is the same every time.
--   This module is coarse. Its lifecycle, its steps and the shape of a price
--   are stated; the figures, the count of search and what fatigue does are
--   open questions, and nothing should be built on them yet.
--   Sources: docs/explanation/solving-sudoku.md, which asks for empirically
--   validated cognitive costs, and the per-technique scale of Sudoku
--   Explainer (N. Juillerat), the likeliest first source of base figures.
--
-- Includes
--   - The run: one for each pricing asked for. It looks, steps and looks
--     again until the grid is full, or until the catalogue itself licenses
--     nothing.
--   - Price: a base figure for the technique, scaled by how much of the
--     player's capacity the deduction fills, plus what it took to find.
--   - Escalation: a step from beyond the profile, taken when nothing within
--     it is left, flagged, and priced like any other.
--   - What a rating reads: the dearest step, the total, the count of steps
--     and the count of escalations, and whether the total passes the
--     player's budget.
--
-- Excludes
--   - Missing and erring. A deduction beyond the profile is dear, never
--     unseen, and every step is sound. So this model reads repertoire,
--     capacity, spans, marking, order, fixation, budget and fatigue, and
--     ignores upkeep and patience.
--   - Hints. A hint is what a player would find, which is reach.allium's.
--   - Time. A price is effort and no clock is read.
--   - Chance, and which of several equally cheap deductions is taken.
--
-- Dependencies
--   sudoku.allium, for Given, and technique.allium, for the grid, the
--   catalogue, deductions and the profile.
--
-- Vocabulary
--   technique.allium's words stand. To them: run, look and step, as in
--   reach.allium, each module's own. Price, what one step costs this player;
--   base figure, what its technique costs anyone. Within, of a deduction the
--   profile reaches; beyond, of one it does not. Escalation, a step from
--   beyond. Unpriced, of a run the catalogue could not finish.

use "./sudoku.allium" as sudoku
use "./technique.allium" as technique

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity Run {
    profile: technique/Profile
    start: Set<sudoku/Given>
    status: looking | stepping | solved | unpriced

    -- A run looks and steps by turns and ends solved, or unpriced where the
    -- puzzle needs something beyond the catalogue: one of the families
    -- technique.allium defers, or a chain past its limits.
    transitions status {
        looking -> stepping
        stepping -> looking
        looking -> solved
        looking -> unpriced
        terminal: solved, unpriced
    }

    grid: technique/Grid with keeper = this

    steps: Step with run = this
    last_steps: steps where is_last
    escalations: steps where is_beyond_profile

    -- What the steps so far have cost.
    total: Decimal

    is_over_budget: total > profile.budget

    -- What reach.allium calls seen. Here it only decides which deductions
    -- are tried first.
    is_within(x): profile.sees(x)

    has_something_within: grid.deductions.any(x => is_within(x))

    -- The profile is exhausted before the run goes beyond it.
    is_eligible(x): is_within(x) or not has_something_within

    -- base_figure is a black box: what the technique costs anyone, from a
    -- table this module has still to state. search_effort is a black box:
    -- what this player examines, in their order and from their fixation,
    -- before the deduction is found. A deduction that fills the player's
    -- capacity costs its base figure, a smaller one a share of it, and one
    -- past capacity more than it.
    price(x):
        base_figure(x.technique) * x.load / profile.capacity
            + search_effort(grid, profile, last_steps, x)

    is_cheapest(x):
        is_eligible(x)
            and grid.deductions.all(o => is_eligible(o) implies price(o) >= price(x))

    is_poised: status = looking and grid != null and grid.is_kept
}

entity Step {
    run: Run
    index: Integer
    deduction: technique/Deduction

    -- Taken from beyond the profile because nothing within it was left.
    is_beyond_profile: Boolean

    -- The price when it was taken.
    cost: Decimal

    is_last: run.steps.all(o => o.index <= index)
    is_dearest: run.steps.all(o => o.cost <= cost)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    side: Integer = sudoku/config.side
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

rule BeginPricing {
    when: Price(givens, profile)

    -- A price is of a puzzle, and only well-posed givens are one.
    requires: solution_count(givens, config.side) = 1

    -- A player who can hold nothing has no price for anything.
    requires: profile.capacity >= 1

    ensures: Run.created(profile: profile, start: givens, status: looking, total: 0)
}

rule OpenGrid {
    when: run: Run.created

    ensures: technique/Grid.created(keeper: run, start: run.start, uniqueness_promised: true)
}

rule KeepMarksTrue {
    when: cell: technique/GridCell.has_stale_candidate

    -- Upkeep is perfect here, as in reach.allium. Whether it should be free
    -- is an open question below.
    for run in Runs where grid = cell.grid:
        requires: run.status = looking

        ensures: cell.candidates = cell.candidates - cell.placed_peer_digits
}

rule Look {
    when: run: Run.is_poised

    requires: run.status = looking
    requires: run.is_poised

    -- Read before anything changes, so that the step about to be recorded
    -- does not enter its own price. chosen of nothing is nothing, and a
    -- binding is read whether or not the branch below uses it, so the
    -- price is guarded: pricing nothing would read the technique of
    -- nothing, which is an error. Then no step is recorded and no price
    -- is read.
    let taken = chosen(filter(run.grid.deductions, x => run.is_cheapest(x)))
    let cost = if taken != null: run.price(taken) else: null
    let next_index = run.steps.count + 1

    -- One rule and three ends. A full grid is solved. A grid that licenses
    -- nothing at all is beyond the catalogue, and the run is unpriced rather
    -- than given a figure that means nothing. Otherwise the cheapest
    -- eligible deduction is taken, at its price. chosen and filter are the
    -- black boxes reach.allium reads.
    ensures:
        if run.grid.is_filled:
            run.status = solved
        else if run.grid.deductions.count = 0:
            run.status = unpriced
        else:
            Step.created(
                run: run,
                index: next_index,
                deduction: taken,
                is_beyond_profile: not run.is_within(taken),
                cost: cost
            )
            run.total = run.total + cost
            run.status = stepping
}

rule TakeStep {
    when: run: Run.status transitions_to stepping

    requires: run.status = stepping

    -- Applied as in reach.allium: the placement put in its cell, or each
    -- strike taken from its cell.
    ensures:
        run.status = looking
        for step in run.last_steps:
            if step.deduction.placement != null:
                for cell in run.grid.cells:
                    if cell.row = step.deduction.placement.position.row
                            and cell.column = step.deduction.placement.position.column:
                        cell.digit = step.deduction.placement.digit
                        cell.candidates = { step.deduction.placement.digit }
            for strike in step.deduction.strikes:
                for cell in run.grid.cells:
                    if cell.row = strike.position.row and cell.column = strike.position.column:
                        cell.candidates = cell.candidates - strike.digits
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant NothingIsSpentBeforeTheFirstStep {
    for run in Runs:
        run.steps.count = 0 implies run.total = 0
}

invariant EscalationsAreBeyondTheProfile {
    for step in Steps:
        step.is_beyond_profile = not step.run.is_within(step.deduction)
}

invariant NoCostIsNegative {
    for step in Steps:
        step.cost >= 0
}

invariant SolvedMeansFilled {
    for run in Runs:
        run.status = solved implies run.grid.is_filled
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface Pricing {
    provides:
        Price(givens, profile)

    @guarantee PricedEndToEnd
        -- A run never stops because the profile gave out. It stops solved,
        -- or unpriced where the catalogue itself licenses nothing, so two
        -- profiles put to one puzzle are compared over the whole of it.
        -- Either end records no step and leaves the total as it stood:
        -- nothing is priced when nothing is taken.

    @guarantee EscalationIsTheLastResort
        -- No step is taken from beyond the profile while anything within it
        -- is licensed, and every such step is flagged.

    @guarantee SameInputSamePrice
        -- The same givens and the same profile give the same steps, the
        -- same costs and the same total, every time.
}

surface PricedRun {
    context run: Run

    exposes:
        run.status
        run.profile
        run.total
        run.is_over_budget
        run.steps.count
        run.escalations.count
        for step in run.steps:
            step.index
            step.deduction
            step.is_beyond_profile
            step.cost
            step.is_last
            step.is_dearest
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "The base figures. Sudoku Explainer's scale is the likeliest start, but it prices a hidden single in a box below one in a line, which here is extent and not technique. One figure per technique, or per technique and extent?"

open question "search_effort: what is counted as examined before a find (units, cells, digits), how order and fixation change it, and whether an unsystematic player pays less search for a dearer find. human-solving.allium's EffortAccounting and ChoiceAndBias answer it for a seeded attempt, one paid inspection at a time; still open is the figure this deterministic model should read, which might be that model's expectation."

open question "fatigue: does every profile.fatigue of effort spent take one from capacity, and does a run that passes profile.budget end, or only report it? In human-solving.allium fatigue raises error and lowers notice and never touches capacity, and the effort limit ends an attempt; the two models need not agree, but the difference should be chosen."

open question "Upkeep is free here. Marking a grid up and striking after each placement is real work for a player who keeps marks; should it be priced, and should a player with no marks pay nothing and find less? human-solving.allium prices every note written and erased."

open question "An unpriced run: what should a rating say of a puzzle the catalogue cannot finish? Every named technique is now specified, so this is a puzzle that needs a deferred family, a chain past technique.allium's limits, or a guess."

open question "Pricing a variable load. For colouring, chains, forcing chains and BUG+1 a deduction's load is the count of candidate propositions in its proof, which may be many times any capacity; base_figure * load / capacity was written for loads of one to four. Is a long chain priced by its length, by what is held at once, or by its base figure alone?"

open question "Should the cheapest deduction be taken, as here, or the one reach.allium would take, priced? The first is the least a puzzle can cost this player; the second is what it would."
